.TH PSDiagonalMask 3 2023-12-09 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSDiagonalMask\fR

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
PSMatrix  
.br
\fBPSDiagonalMask\fR(\fIint size\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a matrix with shape \fIsize\fR, \fIsize\fR diagonally filled with 1.0 from the top-left side to the bottom-right side, example:
.br


PSDiagonalMask(4); // ->
.br
// {1, 0, 0, 0,
.br
//  1, 1, 0, 0,
.br
//  1, 1, 1, 0,
.br
//  1, 1, 1, 1}
.br




.SH RETURN VALUES
The matrix of \fINULL\fR if:

.RS 4
\[bu] \fIsize\fR is less than 1
.br

\[bu] The matrix cannot be allocated in memory.
.br
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1)
